cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Molt: Ab Initio Complex Dielectric Function from AIMD Dipole Trajectories"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Weigand
    given-names: Alysse
    affiliation: "University of Missouri – Kansas City"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
abstract: >-
  Molt computes the complex dielectric function from VASP ab initio molecular
  dynamics trajectories. It builds a quasi-dipole moment time series, computes
  the dipole autocorrelation function, and applies a numerical derivative
  followed by a fast Fourier transform to obtain the real and imaginary parts of
  the permittivity, along with derived optical properties. Because the method
  rests on the fluctuation-dissipation theorem rather than a harmonic expansion,
  the accessible frequency range is set by trajectory length and sampling
  interval rather than by the formalism, reaching the infrared through microwave
  regimes with no experimental input and no Berry-phase polarization. The
  repository also includes VASP validation tooling for structural relaxation,
  AIMD timestep, and Nose-Hoover thermostat mass.
keywords:
  - dielectric function
  - permittivity
  - ab initio molecular dynamics
  - fluctuation-dissipation theorem
  - dipole autocorrelation
  - infrared spectroscopy
  - microwave
  - VASP
  - computational physics
